    },
    {
      "id": "WDHxMiEqWFMvzelQEH5AU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1361.9497202773362,
      "y": 7383.0088800547355,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 900,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1349092458,
      "version": 895,
      "versionNonce": 1785454890,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792206488176,
      "created": 1792167262927,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "FUNC REQ:\n- browser items\n- place order with multiple items\n- track order status\n\nNON FUNC REQ:\n- Many users can browse items, 1M DAU estimated with each doing 20 req\nso 1M x 20 /10^5 = 200 req per sec\n- We should show the items even if only 1 available and multiple user\ncompete for it. later when placing the order we can verify. so\navailability is must and eventual consistency\n- Reliability: 99.9% uptime over time period\n- Performance: p95 latency under 200 ms\n- Security: authenticated users \n\nENTITIES:\n- Customer {id, name, info}\n- Order {id, status, createdAt, userid}\n- OrderItem {orderId, itemId, quantity}\n- Warehouse {id, location..}\n- Item {id, name, price}\n- WarehouseItem {warehouse id, item id, quantity}\n\nAPI:\nGET /v1/item\nbody: {search query with some filters}\nResponse: list of items\n\nPOST /v1/order\nbody: {order containing item list}\nResponse: status as placed and orderId for tracking\n\nGET /v1/order/{orderId}\nResponse: {status and other info}\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "FUNC REQ:\n- browser items\n- place order with multiple items\n- track order status\n\nNON FUNC REQ:\n- Many users can browse items, 1M DAU estimated with each doing 20 req so 1M x 20 /10^5 = 200 req per sec\n- We should show the items even if only 1 available and multiple user compete for it. later when placing the order we can verify. so availability is must and eventual consistency\n- Reliability: 99.9% uptime over time period\n- Performance: p95 latency under 200 ms\n- Security: authenticated users \n\nENTITIES:\n- Customer {id, name, info}\n- Order {id, status, createdAt, userid}\n- OrderItem {orderId, itemId, quantity}\n- Warehouse {id, location..}\n- Item {id, name, price}\n- WarehouseItem {warehouse id, item id, quantity}\n\nAPI:\nGET /v1/item\nbody: {search query with some filters}\nResponse: list of items\n\nPOST /v1/order\nbody: {order containing item list}\nResponse: status as placed and orderId for tracking\n\nGET /v1/order/{orderId}\nResponse: {status and other info}\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
