      "text": "Video Processing System",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Video Processing System",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "pGiufrVonbW4-EupE4Qsx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1227.8429574750085,
      "y": 13970.357005419102,
      "width": 780.6810857494148,
      "height": 800,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bHo",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1504137072,
      "version": 1337,
      "versionNonce": 1403670928,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792350833796,
      "created": 1792337805353,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design a video processing platform where users can upload large videos\nand have them converted into different resolutions (360p, 720p,\n1080p).\nOnce processing finishes, users should be able to stream the processed\nvideos.\nAssume videos can be several GB in size.\n\nFUNC REQ:\n- user should be able to upload videos of diff resolutions\n- we convert the video into 360, 720 and 1080 to store all varients\n- user can stream the video \n\nNON FUNC REQ:\n- scale: 100M DAU; viewing videos >> uploaders \n     viewing - 100M x 5 / 10^5 = 5k reads per sec\n     uploading - 1M x 2 / 10^5 = 20 uploads per sec\n- storage: 2M x 4GB x 356 = 2.4 EB/year\n- fast streaming\n- our system should be highly available\n\nDATA MODEL:\nUser (userId, name...)\nVideo (videoId, userId, uploadedAt, s3Key)\nVideoFormat (formatId, videoId, size, format, status, s3KeySuffix)\n\nAPI:\nPOST /upload -> {s3 presignedUrl}\nbody {video info}\n\nGET /view/{videoId} -> {VideoFormat[]} they can view in any format\n\nGET /upload/status/{videoId} -> {status}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design a video processing platform where users can upload large videos and have them converted into different resolutions (360p, 720p, 1080p).\nOnce processing finishes, users should be able to stream the processed videos.\nAssume videos can be several GB in size.\n\nFUNC REQ:\n- user should be able to upload videos of diff resolutions\n- we convert the video into 360, 720 and 1080 to store all varients\n- user can stream the video \n\nNON FUNC REQ:\n- scale: 100M DAU; viewing videos >> uploaders \n     viewing - 100M x 5 / 10^5 = 5k reads per sec\n     uploading - 1M x 2 / 10^5 = 20 uploads per sec\n- storage: 2M x 4GB x 356 = 2.4 EB/year\n- fast streaming\n- our system should be highly available\n\nDATA MODEL:\nUser (userId, name...)\nVideo (videoId, userId, uploadedAt, s3Key)\nVideoFormat (formatId, videoId, size, format, status, s3KeySuffix)\n\nAPI:\nPOST /upload -> {s3 presignedUrl}\nbody {video info}\n\nGET /view/{videoId} -> {VideoFormat[]} they can view in any format\n\nGET /upload/status/{videoId} -> {status}",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
