      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Whatsapp",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "MkN1Hfl5NFeY-JF0utcj9",
      "originalText": "Whatsapp",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "QY0I4QjlFQ1QIgj4RlS7H",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1233.6609825733535,
      "y": 14890.031762857274,
      "width": 1144,
      "height": 1275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIb",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1242929520,
      "version": 1566,
      "versionNonce": 943843216,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792350829735,
      "created": 1792347806991,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design a real-time messaging system where users can send and receive text messages.\nThe system must support:\n- One-to-one messaging.\n- Delivery to online users in near real time.\n- Storing messages for offline users and delivering them when they reconnect.\n- Retrieving chat history.\nIgnore group chats, media sharing, voice calls, and end-to-end encryption for now.\n\nuser1---message---server----message---user2\n\nFUNC REQ:\n- user should be able to send and receive messages from one another\n- if user is offline then we retain the messages and send them when back online\n- users can load their prev chat history\n\nNON FUNC REQ:\n- scale: 100M DAU ~ each user sends 20 messages per day so we need to store it and send it to other user\n   100M x 20/10^5 = 20k messages per second (being written and streamed in near real time)\n- strong consistency in maintaining user connections \n- high availability \n- near real time streaming; p99 latency under 200ms \n\nDATA MODEL:\nUser (id, name, ...)\nChat (chatId, createAt)\nChatRoom(chatId, userId)\nMessage (mId, userId, chatId, content, timestamp, status, sequenceId)\n\nUserA ------ Chat --- [Messages]\nUserB-------/\n\nChat:\n    UserA: hello 12pm\n    UserB: hi 12:02pm\n    UserB: how are you 12:02pm\n    UserA: sdklf 12:02pm\n    UserB: sdfdf 12:42pm\n\nAPI:\nuser1---message---server----message---user2\n\nClient sends to server and server forwards it to other user based on chatId or we can pass the receiver \n{message, chatId, userId}\n\nResponse from server\n{message, chatId, userId}\n\nfor getting past messages when client comes back online\n/GET /v1/chat/{chatId}/message?before=sequenceNumber?limit=50 -> {message[]}\n\n    ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design a real-time messaging system where users can send and receive text messages.\nThe system must support:\n- One-to-one messaging.\n- Delivery to online users in near real time.\n- Storing messages for offline users and delivering them when they reconnect.\n- Retrieving chat history.\nIgnore group chats, media sharing, voice calls, and end-to-end encryption for now.\n\nuser1---message---server----message---user2\n\nFUNC REQ:\n- user should be able to send and receive messages from one another\n- if user is offline then we retain the messages and send them when back online\n- users can load their prev chat history\n\nNON FUNC REQ:\n- scale: 100M DAU ~ each user sends 20 messages per day so we need to store it and send it to other user\n   100M x 20/10^5 = 20k messages per second (being written and streamed in near real time)\n- strong consistency in maintaining user connections \n- high availability \n- near real time streaming; p99 latency under 200ms \n\nDATA MODEL:\nUser (id, name, ...)\nChat (chatId, createAt)\nChatRoom(chatId, userId)\nMessage (mId, userId, chatId, content, timestamp, status, sequenceId)\n\nUserA ------ Chat --- [Messages]\nUserB-------/\n\nChat:\n    UserA: hello 12pm\n    UserB: hi 12:02pm\n    UserB: how are you 12:02pm\n    UserA: sdklf 12:02pm\n    UserB: sdfdf 12:42pm\n\nAPI:\nuser1---message---server----message---user2\n\nClient sends to server and server forwards it to other user based on chatId or we can pass the receiver \n{message, chatId, userId}\n\nResponse from server\n{message, chatId, userId}\n\nfor getting past messages when client comes back online\n/GET /v1/chat/{chatId}/message?before=sequenceNumber?limit=50 -> {message[]}\n\n    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
