    {
      "id": "ocrZGL4OGpRUK6dwXBWJc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1177.815307556201,
      "y": 16313.393853374577,
      "width": 1153.8051330798478,
      "height": 1025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 342288784,
      "version": 1410,
      "versionNonce": 680226704,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792355951772,
      "created": 1792354468418,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design a simplified version of Twitter (X).\nUsers should be able to publish short text posts, follow other users, and view a personalized home feed\ncontaining posts from the people they follow.\nFor example, if User A follows User B and User C, User A's feed should show posts from B and C, with the\nnewest posts first.\n\nuserA posts 'got a new car' -> [B, C, D] followers\n\nuserB opens feed [userA post, userE post.....] ranked by newest first\n\nFUNC REQ:\n- users should be able to post \n- users can follow each other\n- users can view feed containing posts from followings ranked by newest\n\nNON FUNC REQ:\n- scale: 100M DAU; \neach user posts 1-2 everyday so 100M x 2/10^5 = 2k writes per sec\nusers will view posts on their feed 100M gets feed from 100s of following assuming\n100M x 100/10^5 = 10k reads per sec concurrently approx\n- if usersA posts something we can have slight delay before showing it on the feeds; eventual\nconsistency\n- high availability \n- feed loading latency p95 under 400ms\n\nDATA MODEL:\nUser (userId, name)\nFollow (followerId, followeeId) A->B\nPost (postId, userId, createdAt, content)\n\nAPI:\nPOST /post -> {postId} httpStatus\nbody: {post content}\n\nPUT /follow/{userId} -> success\nwill add new user to following list of curr user\n\nPUT /unfollow/{userId}\n\nGET /post -> {Post[]}\nfeed for curr user",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design a simplified version of Twitter (X).\nUsers should be able to publish short text posts, follow other users, and view a personalized home feed containing posts from the people they follow.\nFor example, if User A follows User B and User C, User A's feed should show posts from B and C, with the newest posts first.\n\nuserA posts 'got a new car' -> [B, C, D] followers\n\nuserB opens feed [userA post, userE post.....] ranked by newest first\n\nFUNC REQ:\n- users should be able to post \n- users can follow each other\n- users can view feed containing posts from followings ranked by newest\n\nNON FUNC REQ:\n- scale: 100M DAU; \neach user posts 1-2 everyday so 100M x 2/10^5 = 2k writes per sec\nusers will view posts on their feed 100M gets feed from 100s of following assuming\n100M x 100/10^5 = 10k reads per sec concurrently approx\n- if usersA posts something we can have slight delay before showing it on the feeds; eventual consistency\n- high availability \n- feed loading latency p95 under 400ms\n\nDATA MODEL:\nUser (userId, name)\nFollow (followerId, followeeId) A->B\nPost (postId, userId, createdAt, content)\n\nAPI:\nPOST /post -> {postId} httpStatus\nbody: {post content}\n\nPUT /follow/{userId} -> success\nwill add new user to following list of curr user\n\nPUT /unfollow/{userId}\n\nGET /post -> {Post[]}\nfeed for curr user",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
